#
# Semantic content of the header page: values, relations and properties.
# The presence of each name and type comes with the Tier 0 generator.

assertion  XBD.errno.h.001
anchor     basedefs/errno.h.html#DESCRIPTION/errno
class      required
since      2001
says       Every error number <errno.h> lists is defined as a positive integer
           constant expression of type int that can be used in #if.
test       t/001-e-constants.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.errno.h.002
anchor     basedefs/errno.h.html#DESCRIPTION/errno
class      required
since      2001
says       The error numbers <errno.h> lists are pairwise different, except that
           EAGAIN and EWOULDBLOCK may be equal and ENOTSUP and EOPNOTSUPP may be
           equal.
note       Equal or different is accepted for the two permitted pairs.
test       t/002-e-distinct.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.errno.h.003
anchor     basedefs/errno.h.html#DESCRIPTION/errno
class      required
since      1988
says       errno expands to a modifiable lvalue of type int: it can be assigned,
           changed in place and have its address taken.
test       t/003-errno-lvalue.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.errno.h.004
anchor     basedefs/errno.h.html#DESCRIPTION/errno
class      required
since      2001
says       errno has thread local storage duration: a value stored by one thread
           is not seen by another thread, and the other thread storing its own
           value does not change it.
note       The value errno has when a thread starts is not required here.
test       t/004-errno-thread-local.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
